//! SWMM 5.2.4 `culvert.c` inlet flows on non-mitered codes, converted to SI.
//!
//! SWMM ran in feet. `swmm_headwater` is its head times 0.3048, `discharge` its flow times
//! 0.3048^3. `reference` is the 100-digit headwater at that discharge on SWMM's own constants
//! (Ku = 1, g = 32.2 ft/s2), converted to metres.
//!
//! `class` is fixed from the code's form and the branch, before any value is compared:
//! - `Agrees`: SWMM evaluates the same equation. `tolerance` is the relative headwater bound
//!   from SWMM's numerics: 1e-12 for box rows, 4 times the relative error of SWMM's 10-digit PI
//!   for circle rows.
//! - `Form1StaleFlow`: unsubmerged row of a form-1 code. SWMM v5.2.4 returns the flow of the
//!   last `form1Eqn` call, not of the root Ridder returns (culvert.c line 358, findroot.c
//!   line 112), so the flow is wrong by up to 47 percent. `replay_discharge` is the bit-exact
//!   replay of that flow. `discharge` must equal it, and the row must miss `reference` by more
//!   than `tolerance`, the relative bound of the `Agrees` rows of the same shape.

